      "abstract": "$\\Lambda$ and $\\bar\\Lambda$ rapidity density as a function of negative hadron multiplicity at mid-rapidity. The open symbols in the figure are data points from an independent analysis of minimum bias data set using event-mixing techniques. Errors shown are statistical only. Systematic errors on hyperon yields $10\\%$, on negative hadron yields $6\\%$. $\\Lambda$ and $\\bar\\Lambda$ measured for $|y|<0.5$, negative hadrons for $|\\eta|<0.1$. Dashed lines correspond to $\\Lambda = 0.054 h^{-}$, $\\bar\\Lambda = 0.040 h^{-}$.",
